{
  "version": "schemaxis.readiness/1",
  "routes": {
    "schemaxis.sox/1": {
      "guide": "docs/sox.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Assemble excerpts of PCM16 recordings with frame-accurate cuts, gains and nonoverlapping linear fades (assemble), or conform one recording to PCM16 mono 16000 Hz for speech recognition (conform), or normalise one recording to an explicit peak level with a measured gain (normalise), or mix a narration and a background recording with explicit gains, sample-frame placements and a duration policy (mix).",
        "assumptions": "Absolute canonical PCM16 little-endian WAV files, mono/stereo, 8000–192000 Hz; assemble needs identical sample rates/channels across clips; conform takes one file and an explicit channelPolicy; latest stable SoX 14.4.2. Normalise takes one file, an integer targetPeak in PCM16 sample units (1 to 32767) and a maxGain boost ceiling (1 to 16). Mix takes two such files with identical rate and channels, a gain 0–4 with at most four decimals and an offsetFrames placement for each, and a required durationPolicy (longest or narration).",
        "constraints": "Assemble: eight clips, 262144 total output frames, 4MiB total source bytes, 1048576 combined scalar samples; no clipping, resampling, mix, crossfade or authored effects. Conform: one source <=32MiB and <=600 seconds, output always PCM16 mono 16000 Hz, no other rates, gain, normalisation, noise reduction or authored options. Normalise: one source <=32MiB and <=600 seconds; the output keeps the source rate, channels and frame count; peak scaling by one exact rational gain only, with no decibel target, loudness/RMS/EBU R128/true-peak control, mixing, resampling, trimming, fades, dither, limiter or authored options. Mix: two sources, 4MiB total source bytes, 262144 output frames, 1048576 combined scalar samples; no resampling, channel conversion, ducking, crossfade, loudness control, limiter, other track counts or authored options; any gained term or exact sum outside PCM16 is refused rather than clipped.",
        "inspection": "Reopen native audio.wav (and assemble per-clip WAVs); standard-library wave/struct and analytic frame envelopes independently check every assemble sample, canonical native output headers and run-directory membership. Conform recomputes same-rate channel conversion exactly, compares resampled output with the source in a declared 0-0.6 Nyquist band through one independent physical-time low-pass at bounded interior instants (not a bit-exact or full-band oracle; SoX's transition/stop band, edges and instants touching native clipping are not compared), and checks rate, channels, frame count, diagnostics and membership. Summaries state exact rate, channels, frames and duration; assemble states segment maps and loses original timestamps, conform keeps the time axis. Normalise: the host measures the peak over all samples, derives the exact gain fraction and refuses silence or over-maxGain boost before SoX starts, then compares every output scalar sample with the exact rational sample*targetPeak/peak (nearest PCM16 integer), requires the output peak to equal targetPeak, empty native stdout/stderr and exact membership; the summary reports the exact gain, headroom, exact maximum error, claims and limits. Mix: the host reopens both captures, both padded intermediates (exact offset silence plus captured samples) and audio.wav, recomputes every output scalar sample as the exact gained sum with integer arithmetic and requires the nearest PCM16 integer (exact ties either way), the policy-implied frame count, empty native stdout/stderr and exact membership; the summary reports tracks, intervals, overlap, peaks and the maximum error.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_AUDIO_FADE: shorten fades. AUDIO_SOURCE_BOUNDS: choose a trim inside source frames, or supply a longer source to conform. AUDIO_CLIPPING: lower gain before fades. AUDIO_FORMAT_MISMATCH: supply equal rate/channels. AUDIO_CHANNEL_POLICY: right was chosen for a mono source; use average or left. MISSING_ARGUMENT/INVALID_ARGUMENT at channelPolicy: choose average, left or right. INVALID_AUDIO_DATA: re-export canonical PCM16. AUDIO_RESOURCE_LIMIT: split the work. INTERPRETER_NOT_FOUND: configure SoX 14.4.2. VERIFICATION_FAILED: injected chunks, unreferenced files, forged summaries/receipts/results or output beyond the declared fidelity limit; rerun from declared input into a fresh directory. AUDIO_SILENT_SOURCE: choose a recording that contains signal. AUDIO_GAIN_LIMIT: lower targetPeak, raise maxGain deliberately or supply a louder recording. INVALID_ARGUMENT/MISSING_ARGUMENT at targetPeak or maxGain: supply an integer 1-32767 and a number 1-16. Mix: AUDIO_FORMAT_MISMATCH: conform one recording or record both alike. AUDIO_CLIPPING: lower a gain or source level. AUDIO_SOURCE_BOUNDS: under durationPolicy narration the background starts at or after the narration end. MISSING_ARGUMENT/INVALID_ARGUMENT at durationPolicy: choose longest or narration. INVALID_ARGUMENT at gain: use 0–4 with at most four decimals."
      },
