          "cancellation": "Shared tracked process-group cancellation terminates owned native jobs; cancellation is checked before publication.",
          "logs": "Authored/effective plans, WAV captures, input hashes, trusted launchers, submissions/stdout/stderr, assemble per-clip WAVs or the conform or normalise stage files, and final audio retained. Mix also retains captured-1.wav and the pad-0.wav and pad-1.wav stage files.",
          "verification": "Strict RIFF and wave/struct reopening, canonical fmt+data native outputs, analytic trim/gain/fade samples within 0.5001 PCM16 LSB (one quantisation plus sub-LSB PCM32 effects), exact integer concatenation, exact command/input/evidence/publication/receipt/result binding and no unreferenced audio or stage files. Conform: strict header and canonical output, exact round-half-up frame count, exact integer channel conversion at 16000 Hz, band-limited projection comparison (0-0.6 Nyquist, bounded interior instants, declared analytic limit; not bit-exact) otherwise, empty stdout, clipping-only stderr, saturation/cancellation/silence warnings, streaming reads with no sample lists. Normalise: strict header, canonical output with the source rate/channels/frames, exact rational comparison of every scalar sample (nearest PCM16 integer, exact integer arithmetic), output peak equal to targetPeak, empty stdout and stderr, bounded pair set and streaming reads with no sample lists. Mix: exact padded-intermediate reopening, exact integer comparison of every output scalar sample with the gained sum (nearest PCM16, ties either way), empty native stdout/stderr and policy-implied frame count."
        },
